<?xml version="1.0"?>
<config xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
        xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="urn:magento:module:Magento_Config:etc/system_file.xsd">
    <system>
        <section id="copex_warrantylabel" translate="label" sortOrder="905"
                 showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
            <label>EU Guarantee Notice &amp; GARAN Label</label>
            <tab>sales</tab>
            <resource>CopeX_WarrantyLabel::config</resource>
            <group id="general" translate="label comment" sortOrder="10"
                   showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                <label>General Settings</label>
                <comment><![CDATA[Implements the EU harmonised notice on the legal guarantee of conformity and the EU GARAN label (Implementing Regulation (EU) 2025/1960, applicable from 27 September 2026). This module does not constitute legal advice.]]></comment>
                <field id="enabled" translate="label comment" type="select" sortOrder="10"
                       showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                    <label>Enable Module</label>
                    <source_model>Magento\Config\Model\Config\Source\Yesno</source_model>
                    <comment>Kill switch: "No" removes every notice and label output for this scope.</comment>
                </field>
                <field id="language" translate="label comment" type="select" sortOrder="20"
                       showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                    <label>Label Language</label>
                    <source_model>CopeX\WarrantyLabel\Model\Source\Language</source_model>
                    <comment>Selects the official notice version and the Your Europe link. Set it explicitly when the store locale does not match the language of the store content.</comment>
                </field>
                <field id="trigger_text" translate="label comment" type="text" sortOrder="30"
                       showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                    <label>Nested Display Button Text</label>
                    <comment>Text of the button that opens the notice in nested mode. Leave empty for the translated default "Your legal guarantee rights".</comment>
                </field>
                <field id="alt_text" translate="label comment" type="text" sortOrder="40"
                       showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                    <label>Notice Alternative Text</label>
                    <comment>Alternative text of the notice image for screen readers and blocked images in emails. Leave empty for the translated default.</comment>
                </field>
                <field id="min_width_px" translate="label comment" type="text" sortOrder="50"
                       showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                    <label>Minimum Notice Width (CSS px)</label>
                    <validate>validate-digits</validate>
                    <comment>The notice is never rendered narrower than this, so its QR code stays at least 2 x 2 cm.</comment>
                </field>
                <field id="excluded_product_types" translate="label comment" type="multiselect" sortOrder="60"
                       showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1" canRestore="1">
                    <label>Product Types Without Legal Guarantee Notice</label>
                    <source_model>CopeX\WarrantyLabel\Model\Source\ProductType</source_model>
                    <can_be_empty>1</can_be_empty>
                    <comment>Non-goods such as gift cards or downloads. Checkout and email show the notice only if the cart or order contains at least one other item.</comment>
                </field>
            </group>
            <group id="notice_placement" translate="label comment" sortOrder="20"
                   showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                <label>Legal Guarantee Notice Placements</label>
                <comment><![CDATA["Direct" shows the complete official notice. "Nested" shows a button that opens the notice in a dialog on the first click (EU guidelines p. 16-19); a stricter interpretation requires the direct display.]]></comment>
                <field id="header" translate="label" type="select" sortOrder="10"
                       showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                    <label>Header</label>
                    <source_model>CopeX\WarrantyLabel\Model\Source\DisplayMode</source_model>
                </field>
                <field id="footer" translate="label" type="select" sortOrder="20"
                       showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                    <label>Footer</label>
                    <source_model>CopeX\WarrantyLabel\Model\Source\DisplayMode</source_model>
                </field>
                <field id="category" translate="label" type="select" sortOrder="30"
                       showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                    <label>Category Page</label>
                    <source_model>CopeX\WarrantyLabel\Model\Source\DisplayMode</source_model>
                </field>
                <field id="search" translate="label" type="select" sortOrder="40"
                       showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                    <label>Search Results</label>
                    <source_model>CopeX\WarrantyLabel\Model\Source\DisplayMode</source_model>
                </field>
                <field id="cart" translate="label" type="select" sortOrder="50"
                       showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                    <label>Shopping Cart</label>
                    <source_model>CopeX\WarrantyLabel\Model\Source\DisplayMode</source_model>
                </field>
                <field id="checkout" translate="label" type="select" sortOrder="60"
                       showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                    <label>Checkout (before Place Order)</label>
                    <source_model>CopeX\WarrantyLabel\Model\Source\DisplayMode</source_model>
                </field>
                <field id="success" translate="label" type="select" sortOrder="70"
                       showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                    <label>Checkout Success Page</label>
                    <source_model>CopeX\WarrantyLabel\Model\Source\DisplayMode</source_model>
                </field>
                <field id="email" translate="label" type="select" sortOrder="80"
                       showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                    <label>Order Confirmation Email</label>
                    <source_model>Magento\Config\Model\Config\Source\Yesno</source_model>
                </field>
                <field id="email_attach" translate="label comment" type="select" sortOrder="90"
                       showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                    <label>Attach the Notice Graphic to the Email</label>
                    <source_model>Magento\Config\Model\Config\Source\Yesno</source_model>
                    <comment>Sends the graphic as a PNG file as well. Independent of the field above: many email clients block remote images, and an attached file stays readable without them.</comment>
                </field>
            </group>
            <group id="garan" translate="label comment" sortOrder="30"
                   showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                <label>EU GARAN Label</label>
                <comment><![CDATA[Shown only for products whose producer offers a commercial guarantee of durability free of charge, for the entire good and for more than two years. Maintain the duration on the product; brand, model identifier and terms URL can come from the settings below. A variant without its own values inherits them from its configurable parent.]]></comment>
                <field id="enabled" translate="label" type="select" sortOrder="10"
                       showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                    <label>Enable GARAN Label</label>
                    <source_model>Magento\Config\Model\Config\Source\Yesno</source_model>
                </field>
                <field id="pdp" translate="label" type="select" sortOrder="20"
                       showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                    <label>Product Page</label>
                    <source_model>CopeX\WarrantyLabel\Model\Source\DisplayMode</source_model>
                    <depends>
                        <field id="enabled">1</field>
                    </depends>
                </field>
                <field id="checkout" translate="label" type="select" sortOrder="30"
                       showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                    <label>Checkout (before Place Order)</label>
                    <source_model>CopeX\WarrantyLabel\Model\Source\DisplayMode</source_model>
                    <depends>
                        <field id="enabled">1</field>
                    </depends>
                </field>
                <field id="success" translate="label" type="select" sortOrder="40"
                       showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                    <label>Checkout Success Page</label>
                    <source_model>CopeX\WarrantyLabel\Model\Source\DisplayMode</source_model>
                    <depends>
                        <field id="enabled">1</field>
                    </depends>
                </field>
                <field id="email" translate="label" type="select" sortOrder="50"
                       showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                    <label>Order Confirmation Email</label>
                    <source_model>Magento\Config\Model\Config\Source\Yesno</source_model>
                    <depends>
                        <field id="enabled">1</field>
                    </depends>
                </field>
                <field id="email_attach" translate="label comment" type="select" sortOrder="51"
                       showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                    <label>Attach the Label Graphics to the Email</label>
                    <source_model>Magento\Config\Model\Config\Source\Yesno</source_model>
                    <comment>Sends one PNG file per labelled item as well, named after its SKU. Independent of the field above.</comment>
                    <depends>
                        <field id="enabled">1</field>
                    </depends>
                </field>
                <field id="brand_source" translate="label comment" type="select" sortOrder="52"
                       showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                    <label>Brand Comes From</label>
                    <source_model>CopeX\WarrantyLabel\Model\Source\BrandSource</source_model>
                    <comment><![CDATA[A brand maintained on the product always wins. Brand and model identifier share one line on the label: a value that is too long is rejected, not shrunk, and the product then shows <strong>no label at all</strong>. Check with <code>bin/magento copex:warranty-label:audit</code>, reason <code>too_long</code>.]]></comment>
                    <depends>
                        <field id="enabled">1</field>
                    </depends>
                </field>
                <field id="brand_attribute" translate="label" type="select" sortOrder="53"
                       showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                    <label>Brand Product Attribute</label>
                    <source_model>CopeX\WarrantyLabel\Model\Source\ProductTextAttribute</source_model>
                    <depends>
                        <field id="enabled">1</field>
                        <field id="brand_source">product_attribute</field>
                    </depends>
                </field>
                <field id="brand_value" translate="label" type="text" sortOrder="54"
                       showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                    <label>Brand</label>
                    <depends>
                        <field id="enabled">1</field>
                        <field id="brand_source">config_value</field>
                    </depends>
                </field>
                <field id="model_source" translate="label comment" type="select" sortOrder="55"
                       showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                    <label>Model Identifier Comes From</label>
                    <source_model>CopeX\WarrantyLabel\Model\Source\ModelIdentifierSource</source_model>
                    <comment><![CDATA[A model identifier maintained on the product always wins over the product name. <strong>Careful with "Product name":</strong> most product names are too long for the label line shared with the brand. A value that does not fit is rejected, not shrunk, and the product then shows <strong>no label at all</strong>. Check with <code>bin/magento copex:warranty-label:audit</code>, reason <code>too_long</code>.]]></comment>
                    <depends>
                        <field id="enabled">1</field>
                    </depends>
                </field>
                <field id="terms_url" translate="label comment" type="text" sortOrder="56"
                       showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                    <label>Guarantee Terms URL</label>
                    <comment>Used for every product without its own URL. Full http:// or https:// address in the store view language.</comment>
                    <depends>
                        <field id="enabled">1</field>
                    </depends>
                </field>
                <field id="attach_terms" translate="label comment" type="select" sortOrder="60"
                       showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                    <label>Attach Guarantee Terms to the Order Confirmation</label>
                    <source_model>Magento\Config\Model\Config\Source\Yesno</source_model>
                    <comment><![CDATA[The guarantee statement must reach the consumer on a durable medium at the latest at delivery (§ 9a (3) KSchG, § 479 (2) BGB); a link to a website is not sufficient (CJEU C-49/11). The file is attached only to orders that contain at least one product with a GARAN label.]]></comment>
                    <depends>
                        <field id="enabled">1</field>
                    </depends>
                </field>
                <field id="terms_file" translate="label comment" type="file" sortOrder="70"
                       showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                    <label>Guarantee Terms File (PDF)</label>
                    <backend_model>Magento\Config\Model\Config\Backend\File</backend_model>
                    <upload_dir config="system/filesystem/media" scope_info="1">copex_warranty_label/terms</upload_dir>
                    <base_url type="media" scope_info="1">copex_warranty_label/terms</base_url>
                    <comment>One document per store view. It must name the goods it covers, e.g. "applies to all products of brand X carrying the GARAN label".</comment>
                    <depends>
                        <field id="enabled">1</field>
                        <field id="attach_terms">1</field>
                    </depends>
                </field>
                <field id="terms_filename" translate="label comment" type="text" sortOrder="80"
                       showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                    <label>Attachment File Name</label>
                    <comment>Name the customer sees in the email. Leave empty for the uploaded file name.</comment>
                    <depends>
                        <field id="enabled">1</field>
                        <field id="attach_terms">1</field>
                    </depends>
                </field>
            </group>
        </section>
    </system>
</config>
